<article class="env-definition" id="03P4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03P4">Definition <span data-tag="03P4">59.23.1</span>.</a> On any of the sites $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $ or $S_\tau $ of Section <a href="/tag/03X7" data-tag="03X7">59.20</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The sheaf $T \mapsto \Gamma (T, \mathcal{O}_ T)$ is denoted $\mathcal{O}_ S$, or $\mathbf{G}_ a$, or $\mathbf{G}_{a, S}$ if we want to indicate the base scheme. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Similarly, the sheaf $T \mapsto \Gamma (T, \mathcal{O}^*_ T)$ is denoted $\mathcal{O}_ S^*$, or $\mathbf{G}_ m$, or $\mathbf{G}_{m, S}$ if we want to indicate the base scheme. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>constant sheaf</em> $\underline{\mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}}$ on any site is the sheafification of the constant presheaf $U \mapsto \mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>